 "notes": "Old k24 Flashlight (230 models) split by form into EDC, Tactical, Thrower, Right-angle and Duty kinds; Dive light added as a new kind with types only (no attested models). Family models became archetype versions (SureFire 6P/WeaponLight/G2X/M6/Z2, ProTac, Stinger, Maglite D-cell, Mini Maglite, Kel-Lite, MX-991/U, Baton, PD35, Seeker, Warrior, Nitecore EDC, Tiny Monster, L19, Convoy S2+, Waypoint, Solitaire). Left out: 'Angle-head flashlight' (generic, no maker; it is now the Right-angle kind); Shadowhawk '10000 High Lumens' and GearLight S1000 (listing noise); Klein Tools 'Rechargeable LED Flashlight with Work Light', Fenix WT26RM, Streamlight Bear Trap, Flipmate, Jr. F-Stop, Speedlocker, Syclone and Enduro, Olight Array, Wurkkos HD10 (work, clip or head lights: belong to the Work light / Headlamps shelves); Olight ArkPro, Beagle, Drever, Mettle, Nightclaw, Rubato 4, Sigurd, Splint, Fenix C7 V2, E06R Pro RG, E08R UE, UC30, Ledlenser TT3R, Maglite XL50, Sofirn SP31, SP32A, SP33 (form not confirmed or minor variants; EDC list at 40-model cap). Weapon lights are a type of Tactical flashlight (SureFire WeaponLight archetype, Olight Valkyrie/Baldr in m); E4 may cross-link. Mini Maglite placed under EDC (pocket 2AA), Solitaire under Keychain light. Not done (no page retrieved): archetypes for Ledlenser P7, Convoy C8, Fenix TK, Streamlight SL-20, Olight Perun, LEP throwers. Brand founding years left blank unless on a retrieved page or reliably known."
